    "_historyFieldsNote": "handledByUserId / releasedAt / taskType added app-level (2026-09-27) for the Qnomy Ticket History page. The two release fields stay null here because these six are the live Waiting queue, untouched by this change. handledByUserId is deliberately NOT the same as agentInDxpSessionId: that field is nulled on Finish/Abandon (see SessionReferenceNumbers.tsx), which is correct for 'is this actively held right now' but left the dataset unable to answer 'who served this ticket' once released - exactly the gap qnomyQueueStore.ts's own comment on customersServed already named. taskType is an OPTIONAL override of the queue-level purpose (JOURNEY_PURPOSE_LABELS): a Care & Complaints ticket can be a technical issue or a service request without needing a new queue, so this is a ticket-level refinement, not a replacement for journeyCode. None of these four values (New Postpaid Connection / Billing Issue / Technical Issue / Troubleshooting / Service Request) is evidenced in the corpus beyond the journey-level purpose labels already sourced from the BRSD/journeyCatalogue - this is a demo taxonomy, not a confirmed Qnomy ticket-type vocabulary."
